* Sat Sep 05 2026 fravaccaro 0.5.2-1
- The document list no longer breaks apart when the app is left and come back
  to: the list is read again in place, so what was filed since appears at the
  top, what was deleted goes, and the list stays where it was being read
  instead of starting halfway down the archive
- Reaching the end of the list asks for the next page once and only once, and a
  page is only ever added to the list it was asked for
- Picking a tag or a correspondent shows the documents straight away, as
  picking a view already did, instead of leaving the filters page in front
- A search now runs inside whatever the list is showing, and the search field
  says so: searching while the inbox or a correspondent is picked searches
  those documents rather than starting over on the whole archive
- A list that could not be read again keeps the documents it has, and says why
  instead of emptying itself
- The whole app now works on one list of documents, and the cover reads the
  number of documents in the inbox from the tag itself rather than by listing
  the inbox on the side

* Wed Sep 02 2026 fravaccaro 0.5.1-1
- Only files Paperless can take are offered: the picker lists PDFs, pictures
  and plain text files, other apps offer Paperiton for those kinds only, and a
  file of another kind is turned down with the reason instead of being sent
- The Upload button works again: files picked in the app and files shared with
  it now reach the server instead of staying on the page
- A finished upload names the document it created again, so it can be opened
  from the queue, and the queue and the task list show what the server said
  about a file it could not take
- Documents filed on the same day now keep a fixed order, so refreshing the
  list no longer shows some documents twice while hiding others
- Signing out returns to the sign-in page instead of leaving the settings in
  front, also when the page is left while the countdown runs
- Picking a file to upload and receiving one from another app work again: the
  app now asks for the permissions the file picker and those files need
- "Save on device" puts the archived PDF straight into Downloads, without
  asking for a name first
- Italian interface, and an Italian description where other apps offer to share
  a file with Paperiton
- An upload is followed by a notification with a progress bar and ends as one
  summary, instead of a message per file
- New About page, reached from the pulley menu of the filters page, with the
  licence, the people behind the app and where to send feedback
- A page crediting the translators, and a link to the Transifex project for
  anyone who wants to add a language
- After the app has been used for a while, it asks once whether you want to
  support its development
- New application icon: the document on the Sailfish launcher shape, in the
  green of Paperless-ngx
- The cover carries the document as a faded backdrop that follows the ambience,
  and shows what is waiting: files being uploaded, documents in the inbox, or
  the size of the archive

* Tue Sep 01 2026 fravaccaro 0.5-1
- Sign in through the web interface, so that single sign-on and two-factor
  authentication work; the API token is kept in Sailfish Secrets
- Upload files from the device, from other apps and from the camera, and
  follow the consumer task until the document exists
- Edit title, correspondent, type, tags, date, archive serial number and
  custom fields, and change several documents at once
- Notes, saved views, inbox and the task queue of the server
- Documents are shown inside the app from the private cache directory, which is
  emptied when the app closes and when you sign out; "Save on device" keeps a
  copy in Documents, as the archived PDF or as the file that was uploaded
- Saved files and finished uploads are announced with a notification, the
  filter page marks the view in use, and the document list keeps its place
  when you come back to the app

* Tue Sep 01 2026 fravaccaro 0.1-1
- Initial release: token login, document browsing, search, tag and
  correspondent filters, thumbnails, OCR text and previews
